face-image: img/ev_trade.svg

= Lifting the Sanctions

The sanctions imposed after Naboo are hurting the Trade Federation, and the Federation has been generous to many senators. A motion to lift them is before the Senate, [? if pal_chancellor : with the Chancellor's quiet blessing ?][? if not pal_chancellor : with the support of the Commerce Guilds ?].

- @oppose: Oppose lifting the sanctions.
- @accept: Accept it in the interest of galactic commerce.
- @reparations: Demand full reparations to Naboo first.

@oppose
subtitle: The guilds will retaliate; the corporate worlds grow restless.
on-arrival: guild_relation -= 8; corporate_sep += 2; faith += 0.5

The Caucus fights the motion. The sanctions are softened, not lifted.

@accept
subtitle: The guilds are grateful; it looks like a sell-out.
on-arrival: guild_relation += 6; corruption += 1; guild_embargo -= 1; rimward_dissent += 4; sanctions_lifted = 1; guild_patience += 10

The sanctions end. Within months, the Federation's battleships are back on the trade lanes.

@reparations
subtitle: Naboo is grateful; the guilds grudgingly pay.
on-arrival: guild_relation -= 4; midrim_rc += 1.5; faith += 0.5

The sanctions are lifted only after reparations to Naboo are paid in full.
